# `gg check` must reject an undefined type name in a variable declaration.
# Previously `Floobar x = 5` silently degraded to `error_id` → defaulted to
# unit, so `gg check` reported "OK" and the program either ran wrong or hit a
# C "void value not ignored" link error. The Rust-style numeric shorthand `u8`
# (not a Gorget keyword — `uint8`/`byte` are) gets a "did you mean?" hint.
# See docs/plans/trackB_T4_unknown_type_error.md.

void main():
    Floobar x = 5
    u8 n = 2
    print("unreachable")
